**Improved question:** Instead of "which activities depend on which, and which can run at the same time?", the more useful question here is: *"Which activities require a shared piece of equipment to be prepared before its first use, and which pairs of steps across the two partners' tracks must land on the same instant so a swap happens with zero idle time?"* This surfaces two things the text implies but never states as a discrete activity: (1) the barbell has to be loaded before the very first bench press (mentioned once, in passing, as part of "Partner A loads the bar and does a set..."), which is genuine setup time distinct from the lift itself; and (2) every rest step and every cooldown-start is really a **barrier** — it can only begin once *both* partners have finished their half of the round, not just the partner on that track. That second finding is handled with `compound`/`all` triggers pulling in the sibling track's last step, not with a new step. The first finding adds one inferred step, `load-barbell`, occupying the `bench` task before `bench-press-a-r1`.

